# Plant Shaman

**Alignments.** Any, but tends to be good, unprincipled or aberrant.

The Plant Shaman takes plant life as his totem and shares part of his spirit
potential with the spirits of trees, flowers, grasses and vines, gaining a
kinship that lets him talk with plants, heal them and learn their secrets -
herbs and natural medicines among them. He knows by instinct everything a
farmer''s almanac could tell him, and his magic is limited to spells that touch
plants, earth and animals, plus a handful of conventional ones. Like every
Shaman, his spells are gifts of the spirits rather than learned incantations.

## Lore

Shamans are chosen by the spirits, usually at a brush with death, where a
powerful spirit offers the gift; some are hereditary, tutored from childhood by
a parent and the spirits. A Shaman who abuses the gift risks Bad Medicine from
vengeful spirits. Plant and Animal Shamans often travel together, restoring the
balance of game and forage in places that have lost it. About three in five
Shamans are men.

## Equipment the catalog cannot hold yet

Ceremonial garments and a ceremonial headdress or mask, a hat or hooded cloak,
moccasins, a shovel, a hand axe, 50 feet of rope, a ball of string, a week of
dried food, a small mixing bowl, a grinding stone, sewing needles, thread and
1D4 sticks of charcoal. Two S.D.C. weapons of choice, usually a staff, walking
stick, spear or war club.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'plant-shaman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'plant-shaman';

